/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A pitot tube points into the relative airflow.
   - q is impact pressure in Pa; P0 is total pressure in Pa; P is static pressure in Pa; ρ is air density in kg/m³; V is the speed for which that impact pressure is produced at density ρ.
   - q = ½ρV² holds for incompressible flow, roughly below Mach 0.3 (about 200 kt at sea level); at higher speed the airspeed indicator needs a compressibility correction.
   - In the airspeed indicator, a thin capsule feels P0 on one side and P on the other.
   - The dial shows indicated airspeed (IAS).
   - The altimeter uses a sealed aneroid capsule with a near vacuum inside.
   - The subscale knob sets the reference pressure in the small window.
   - Pressure altitude is not true altitude.
   - No pressure instrument is perfect.
*/
