/* book Worked example: Q: (a) At sea level, where air density is 1.225 kg/m³, an aircraft has an impact pressure of 2500 Pa. Find the indicated airspeed in m/s and in knots. Use 1 m/s = 1.94384 kt. (b) The altimeter subscale is set to 1013.25 hPa and the static pressure outside is 950 hPa. Find the pressure altitude, using 27 ft per hPa.
   1. (a) Use q = ½ρV², so V = √(2q/ρ).
   2. 2q = 2 × 2500 = 5000 Pa.
   3. 2q/ρ = 5000 / 1.225 = 4081.63 m²/s².
   4. V = √4081.63 = 63.89 m/s ≈ 63.9 m/s.
   5. In knots: 63.89 × 1.94384 = 124.2 kt.
   6. (b) Pressure difference = 1013.25 − 950 = 63.25 hPa.
   7. Height = 63.25 × 27 = 1707.75 ft ≈ 1707.8 ft, about 1710 ft.
   Answer: The airspeed is about 63.9 m/s (124 kt), and the pressure altitude is about 1708 ft (roughly 1710 ft). */
