/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Engine speed is measured in revolutions per minute (rpm), but the cockpit usually shows a percentage.
   - A mechanical tachometer takes a flexible drive shaft from the engine gearbox to the indicator.
   - A DC tacho-generator is a small generator driven by the engine shaft.
   - A magnetic or variable-reluctance pickup is better for modern engines.
   - f is pulse frequency in hertz (pulses per second); rpm is shaft speed in revolutions per minute; N is the number of teeth on the wheel.
   - An exhaust gas temperature (EGT) system uses a thermocouple.
   - VTC is thermocouple voltage (µV); S is sensitivity (about 41 µV/°C for type K); Thot is hot-junction temperature (°C); Tcold is cold-junction temperature (°C).
   - The equation shows why the cold junction cannot be ignored: the sensor reports a difference, not an absolute temperature.
   - The display shows EGT.
   - Three readings matter.
*/
