/* book Worked example: Q: A magnetic pickup faces a gear with 30 teeth on the HP shaft of a turbofan. The indicator reads 9000 rpm. (a) Find the pulse frequency in hertz. (b) A type K thermocouple with sensitivity 41 microvolt per degree Celsius has its hot junction at 700 °C and its cold junction at 25 °C. The amplifier gain is 100. Find the voltage reaching the converter in volts.
   1. Convert rpm to revolutions per second: 9000 ÷ 60 = 150 rev/s.
   2. One pulse per tooth per revolution, so f = 150 × 30 = 4500 pulses/s = 4500 Hz.
   3. Temperature difference: 700 − 25 = 675 °C.
   4. Thermocouple voltage: 41 × 675 = 27 675 µV.
   5. Convert to millivolts: 27 675 ÷ 1000 = 27.675 mV.
   6. Amplifier output: 27.675 × 100 = 2767.5 mV = 2.7675 V.
   Answer: (a) 4500 pulses per second (4500 Hz). (b) 2.7675 V reaches the converter. */
