/* book exam traps: Adding the regulator resistance in the load circuit instead of the field circuit. | Treating the vibrating contact as a fixed resistor; it works by duty cycle. | Using no-load voltage in the denominator of regulation; use full-load voltage. | Saying carbon-pile resistance rises with pressure; it falls. And "no contacts" does not mean no wear: the discs wear and drift. | Confusing a cut-out with a regulator; a cut-out removes the generator, a regulator holds voltage. */
